author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "A CI check computes the rendered top-level command set and the contracted command set and fails when the rendered set is not a subset of the contracted set, naming every offending spelling; The check runs in the same job as the existing contracts drift check and cannot be satisfied by regenerating artifacts alone; pm workspace and every one of its actions gain contract entries covering flags, actions, and result shape, verified by pm contracts --command workspace resolving instead of exiting 2; Package-contributed and extension-contributed commands are held to the same invariant, so an install cannot introduce an uncontracted rendered command; The self-referential pm spelling is either contracted or explicitly declared as an exempt alias in contract data, so the exemption is machine-readable rather than a known quirk; A negative-control fixture registers a rendered command with no contract entry and proves the gate fails on it"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Workspace and every rendered user-facing command have contract coverage, with raw-output diagnostics and a snapshot parity gate."
expected_result: All rendered user-facing commands resolve through machine-readable contracts and drift failures include actionable subprocess evidence.
actual_result: Workspace and every rendered command resolve through contracts; the gate fails on omissions and exposes raw invalid-JSON output.
